   Tugindia -- TUGIndia Mailing List


   About Tugindia English (USA)

   This is the general mailing list of the Indian TeX Users Group. The
   main objectives are technical help, propagation of TeX, co-ordination
   of regional chapters and general discussion on sociology and economics
   of free/open software.
     * Talk politely on-list. If you can't be polite, please consider
       unsubscribing.
     * Please don't post any off-topic mail to this list.
     * In your reply, quote only minimum relevant portions of the earlier
       mail. Trim your posts as far as possible and don't top post.
     * Once a 'thread' is declared closed by the moderators, please don't
       insist on discussing it.
     * Personal mail, meant for just 2-3 persons on-list, should not be
       posted to everybody on the list.
     * Signatures and mast-heads should be of reasonable size. LOST tips,
       being informative and 'on topic' here, are welcome.
     * If material is available on the web, post the URL with a small
       description of the same.
     * Don't post only URLs without giving at least a brief idea of what
       the site contains. Some of our readers might not have speedy Net
       access.
     * Don't repeat the same posting more than once to this list.
     * If you find a good TeX-related newsletter which can be
       subscribed-to via the web, send in a brief synopsis of the
       newsletter and directions on how to subscribe to the same.
     * If you find something that would be of interest in a newsletter,
       send across the excerpts of the relevant snippets.
     * Try to condense information and post. This is needed in view of
       the growing number of members on this list.
     * Rather than curse the darkness, light a lamp. If you feel this
       list could be better off with more useful information circulated
       through it, please post something that others would learn from.
     * Commercial postings (in moderate length), must necessarily go with
       the [COMMERCIAL] tag on the subject-line. Such postings should
       preferably be occasional, and not too frequent.
     * If anyone violates these rules (i) lodge a protest, if any, only
       with the moderators, and not directly to the list as a whole (ii)
       preferably send a copy to the person who's behaviour you see as
       violative to the letter and spirit of these rules.

